### Base Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Test /auto root GET
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto
Accept: text/plain

### 2. Test /auto/ with trailing slash
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/
Accept: text/plain

### 3. Test /auto/hello
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/hello
Accept: text/plain

### 4. Test /auto/hello/{name} (e.g., senol)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/hello/senol
Accept: text/plain

### 5. Test /auto/sum/{number1}/{number2} (Valid Integers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/sum/10/5
Accept: application/json

### 6. Test /auto/sum/{number1}/{number2} (Floats)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/sum/12.5/2.5
Accept: application/json

### 7. Test /auto/sum/{number1}/{number2} (Invalid Input Validation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/sum/abc/5
Accept: application/json

### 8. Test /auto/main (Main View Page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/main
Accept: text/html

### 9. Test /auto/about (About View Page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auto/about
Accept: text/html

### 10. Test Top-Level Landing Page (/)
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: text/html

### 11. Test Top-Level About Page (/about)
GET {{baseUrl}}/about
Accept: text/html

### 12. Test Alumni Directory Endpoint (/alumni)
GET {{baseUrl}}/alumni
Accept: application/json

### 13. Test Generic POST Skeleton with JSON Payload
POST {{baseUrl}}/auto
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "action": "test_ping",
    "sender": "qa_client",
    "params": {
        "status": "ready"
    }
}

### 14. Test Generic POST Skeleton with Form Payload
POST {{baseUrl}}/auto
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

action=form_submit&name=Senol&department=MIS

### 15. Web: List Users View (GET /users)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: text/html

### 16. Web: Form Submission - Create User (POST /users)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

first_name=Mehmet&last_name=Celik&email=mehmet.celik@example.com&role=alumni&is_verified=1

### 17. API: List All Users (GET /api/users)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 18. API: Get Single User By ID (GET /api/users/1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

### 19. API: Create New User (POST /api/users)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "Selin",
    "last_name": "Acar",
    "email": "selin.acar@example.com",
    "role": "student",
    "is_verified": 1
}

### 20. API: Update Existing User (PUT /api/users/1)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "first_name": "Admin (Updated)",
    "role": "super_admin"
}

### 21. API: Delete User (DELETE /api/users/5)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/5
Accept: application/json
